WEBVTT

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:10.119
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday the twenty-second. Can you all hear me? We've got the usual lovely echo from the plant end.</v>

00:00:12.099 --> 00:00:20.500
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, clear enough. Before we start, whose new car is that in the car park? It's taking up a fairly ambitious amount of space.</v>

00:00:21.769 --> 00:00:25.269
<v Marcus Hale>Not mine. Mine's the one held together by road dirt.</v>

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:31.399
<v Fiona Doyle>Someone's doing all right, then. Unlike the broken coffee machine in the canteen. Still dispensing disappointment.</v>

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.890
<v Hannah Price>Hot disappointment, or has that bit failed as well?</v>

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a vehicle survey—</v>

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:50.140
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, last thing. The charity bake sale on Friday. Hopefully the cakes are better than the coffee. Not volunteering for anything, just saying.</v>

00:00:51.469 --> 00:00:52.869
<v Grace Liu>Very carefully worded, Fiona.</v>

00:00:54.759 --> 00:01:00.359
<v Sarah Okafor>Practised, I'd say. Right, what's already closed? Keep that separate from what we're agreeing this morning.</v>

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:08.200
<v Fiona Doyle>Already swapped the filter on the waste heat boiler yesterday. That's done, not another one for today.</v>

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:11.049
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, that one's behind us.</v>

00:01:11.579 --> 00:01:19.980
<v Fiona Doyle>And I signed off the inspection on the Line 1 Mould Temperature Controller on Tuesday. That can stay in the finished pile as well.</v>

00:01:21.609 --> 00:01:26.159
<v Hannah Price>Yep, that's the sign-off I was thinking of. Nothing outstanding from that inspection.</v>

00:01:28.019 --> 00:01:33.269
<v Grace Liu>Finished the repair on the line one HPU last night, too. Just reporting completion there.</v>

00:01:35.099 --> 00:01:37.549
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, thanks, Grace. Access and parts blockers?</v>

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:44.939
<v Priya Raman>Um, can't get to the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit until production gives us a window. That's still blocked.</v>

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:51.989
<v Grace Liu>Separate point from the repair I've just mentioned, yeah? Don't want those getting rolled into one.</v>

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:58.189
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, separate. I'm not committing to getting in there today; we haven't got access.</v>

00:01:58.739 --> 00:02:05.040
<v Marcus Hale>And I'm still waiting on parts for the main isolation valve. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:02:06.709 --> 00:02:10.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Both stay as blockers, not fresh jobs being handed out here.</v>

00:02:13.069 --> 00:02:20.770
<v Priya Raman>One observation as well: saw the pressure on the relief valve dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.439
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, talked over the end there. Came back without anyone touching it?</v>

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:32.430
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, on its own. Just passing on what I saw, not proposing another job.</v>

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, observation only. Let's get onto the actual actions.</v>

00:02:37.969 --> 00:02:41.819
<v Sarah Okafor>Olumide, can you order spare parts for the Site Water System?</v>

00:02:42.599 --> 00:02:48.199
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I can't take the ordering on, sorry. I haven't got the capacity for that as well.</v>

00:02:50.219 --> 00:02:55.819
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, fair enough. Fiona, can you take that instead—order spare parts for the Site Water System?</v>

00:02:57.759 --> 00:03:03.009
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll take that from Olumide. I'll order spare parts for the Site Water System.</v>

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:10.030
<v Marcus Hale>That's separate from my main isolation valve parts, just so we're not muddling the two.</v>

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:16.219
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, Site Water System ordering is mine. Your parts wait is still the blocker you mentioned.</v>

00:03:16.699 --> 00:03:20.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Next, the risk assessment for work on the outfeed conveyor needs updating.</v>

00:03:22.259 --> 00:03:28.210
<v Grace Liu>I'll update the risk assessment for work on the outfeed conveyor by end of day. It's urgent.</v>

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.949
<v Hannah Price>Is that the assessment for the work, rather than adding any physical conveyor work to this list?</v>

00:03:37.719 --> 00:03:42.969
<v Grace Liu>Exactly. The risk assessment is what I'm taking. Not volunteering anyone for extra conveyor work.</v>

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:47.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Grace. Urgent, by end of day. Clear.</v>

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:57.110
<v Priya Raman>Yeah so, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the Gas Turbine 2 by Thursday. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:58.439 --> 00:04:03.340
<v Marcus Hale>Thursday as in today, PR? Just checking, because my head's still somewhere around Tuesday.</v>

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:09.669
<v Priya Raman>Today, yes. By Thursday, not next week. Important, but it isn't an urgent one.</v>

00:04:12.039 --> 00:04:16.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed, PR. Permit to work and isolation for the Gas Turbine 2 with you.</v>

00:04:18.439 --> 00:04:22.990
<v Marcus Hale>Right. I heard 'Gas Turbine 2' and nearly jumped in before you'd finished.</v>

00:04:24.399 --> 00:04:28.600
<v Priya Raman>You and half the microphone, yeah. But that's the scope I've taken.</v>

00:04:30.899 --> 00:04:39.300
<v Fiona Doyle>I'll check the guarding on the Injection Moulding Line 1 as well. Not an emergency but don't let it slip—that's how I'm treating it.</v>

00:04:40.009 --> 00:04:44.910
<v Grace Liu>Just the guarding check, Fiona, not agreeing alterations off the back of this call?</v>

00:04:46.769 --> 00:04:52.019
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, checking the guarding on the Injection Moulding Line 1. No alterations being agreed here.</v>

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:56.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Fiona, that's yours. Not an emergency, but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:07.550
<v Hannah Price>There's also the need to recalibrate the sensors on the boiler safety valve tomorrow at 9:30. That's marked low priority. I haven't got an owner for it.</v>

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:11.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Who can take that recalibration? Anyone able to commit?</v>

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:14.589
<v Priya Raman>I can't take it on, sorry.</v>

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:18.120
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, I can't commit to that either.</v>

00:05:20.149 --> 00:05:22.600
<v Marcus Hale>Not one I can take, I'm afraid.</v>

00:05:23.019 --> 00:05:29.670
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, nobody's taking it. Recalibrate the sensors on the boiler safety valve stays unassigned: tomorrow at 9:30, low priority.</v>

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:35.279
<v Hannah Price>And that time is the requested time, not us saying somebody's booked to do it.</v>

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:41.509
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. It's needed, but there's no owner and no commitment to carrying it out.</v>

00:05:43.199 --> 00:05:48.800
<v Olumide Adeyemi>What I can take is the toolbox talk. I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team.</v>

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.990
<v Grace Liu>Where's that sitting priority-wise, Olumide?</v>

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:55.779
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Low priority. I'll organise it, but it's not an urgent one.</v>

00:05:56.899 --> 00:06:00.050
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Olumide. Toolbox talk organisation with you, low priority.</v>

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:07.579
<v Fiona Doyle>That all sounds right from my end. And nobody's accidentally given me the coffee machine, which is a relief.</v>

00:06:08.639 --> 00:06:12.139
<v Hannah Price>Definitely not. That was a complaint, not a maintenance request.</v>

00:06:13.009 --> 00:06:14.410
<v Marcus Hale>A very well-supported complaint.</v>

00:06:16.569 --> 00:06:19.019
<v Sarah Okafor>Anything we've misunderstood in what's been agreed?</v>

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:22.600
<v Grace Liu>No, clear here. Finished work separate, blockers separate.</v>

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:25.709
<v Priya Raman>Same here. All clear.</v>

00:06:27.399 --> 00:06:29.850
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. We'll leave it there. Thanks, everyone.</v>
